+		// Single Custom View production render. ExportRenderingImage always renders every Custom View configured for
+		// the project; these render exactly ONE Custom View for exactly ONE colorway. They drive the same V-Ray
+		// production-render path as ExportRenderingImage (same camera, display state, quality and render settings) -
+		// the render is merely scoped to one view, so there is no separate or degraded code path.
+		//
+		// Render settings other than the view and the colorway (resolution, format, light preset, background, ...)
+		// are the project's current render properties, exactly as with ExportRenderingImage. Added as non-pure
+		// virtuals at the END of the interface so existing implementers / ABI consumers are unaffected.
+		// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+		/// @ingroup EXPORT_API
+		/// @fn ExportRenderingImageForCustomView(const std::string& _filePath, int _customViewIndex, int _colorwayIndex)
+		/// @brief Renders and exports exactly ONE Custom View - addressed by its index in the project's Custom View
+		///        list - for exactly ONE colorway. No other configured output view of the project is rendered and no
+		///        other file is written.
+		/// @param _filePath: output image path including the extension (.png / .jpg), e.g. "C:/out/front.png".
+		/// @param _customViewIndex: Custom View index, 0 to (number of Custom Views - 1). See GetCustomViewInformation().
+		/// @param _colorwayIndex: colorway index (0 to n-1). -1, or any out-of-range index, uses the current colorway.
+		/// @return The written image path, or an empty string on failure - index out of range, no Custom View exists,
+		///         no colorway, a render already in progress, or a build without the V-Ray renderer. Nothing is
+		///         rendered and no file is written in any of those cases.
+		/// @note The image is written to _filePath exactly as given - unlike ExportRenderingImage, the Custom View
+		///       name is NOT appended to the file name. The returned path is still the authoritative one.
+		virtual std::string ExportRenderingImageForCustomView(const std::string& _filePath, int _customViewIndex, int _colorwayIndex) { return std::string(); }
